    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ebb62245_2162437a",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/Buffer.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-13T13:10:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you all expand on what you mean by memory type here? All the backends have a pretty different sense on how they enumerate their memory types and what each means in terms of performance. Personally I feel like its best for the uses of buffers to describe how they intend to use the buffer and then we get the correct memory.\n\nMichael how do you expect a buffer pool to use memory type?",
      "parentUuid": "f1dabe97_367ab87b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "42ac84617be1f5bb35949cf607a66601b0d70c6c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "462f0d7e_e945bc11",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/Buffer.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-13T14:10:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, all the use cases I can think of are actually captured by the BufferType and transient-ness. I had thought (w/o really knowing the details) that if there was a common memory type representation that was a bit more nuanced than transient-ness, it wouldn\u0027t hurt (e.g. static, stream, dynamic). But if there isn\u0027t a unified representation that makes sense across all backends, then I\u0027m fine with this level of detail.\n\nHowever, I do agree with Jim that the current type name is a little misleading, or easy to misinterpret. To me TransientGpuBuffer makes me think the value is actually a buffer. What if we renamed it MemoryType, and it had values kTransient and k[GPU?]Persistent?",
      "parentUuid": "ebb62245_2162437a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "42ac84617be1f5bb35949cf607a66601b0d70c6c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "44f5264a_b1819646",
        "filename": "experimental/graphite/src/Buffer.h",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-13T14:16:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah total fine with finding a better name. I don\u0027t like using MemoryType as the class name though because that suggests the caller is requesting a specific memory type. In reality the caller is just expressing that they want to prioritize reading the buffer on the GPU over anything else. But this can actually be done with different memory types depending on the platform. For example, on Vulkan we will use a GPU_ONLY memory type on desktop, but on mobile we use the regular cpu and gpu accessible memory type. The reason being there is no performance difference on mobile gpus for the memory reads, so by using the cpu_gpu one we save having to do the extra gpu copy.\n\nenum class PrioritizeGpuBufferReads : bool {\n   kNo,\n   kYes,\n}",
      "parentUuid": "462f0d7e_e945bc11",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 22
      },
      "revId": "42ac84617be1f5bb35949cf607a66601b0d70c6c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
